Ported from rules_pycross tests/e2e/patches_and_hooks. Retargeted at the
installed venv layout: rules_py applies post-install patches with `patch -d`
rooted at the install tree, so paths are `lib/python<X.Y>/site-packages/...`
rather than the wheel-relative paths rules_pycross uses. The `PATCHED = True`
context line comes from the pre-build patch, so this hunk only applies when
the two phases ran in order.
--- a/lib/python3.12/site-packages/setproctitle/__init__.py
+++ b/lib/python3.12/site-packages/setproctitle/__init__.py
@@ -56,3 +56,4 @@
 if sys.platform == "darwin":
     getproctitle()
 PATCHED = True
+POST_PATCHED = True
